* Adopted Children:
** {{ill|Tokugawa Iesato|en|Tokugawa Iesato|WD=Q672741|lt=Tokugawa Iesato|1=Tokugawa Iesato}} (1863-1940) adopted son, who became 16th head of the Tokugawa Clan, after the end of the Shogunate dynasty.

His grandson Tokugawa Hiromi graduated as part of the 65th Class of the {{ill|Imperial Japanese Naval Academy|en|Imperial Japanese Naval Academy|WD=Q2238519|lt=Imperial Japanese Naval Academy|1=Imperial Japanese Naval Academy}} in March 1938. On July 12, 1943, he was {{ill|Killed in action|en|Killed in action|WD=Q210392|lt=Killed in action|1=Killed in action}} during {{ill|Pacific War|en|Pacific War|WD=Q184425|lt=Pacific War|1=Pacific War}} when the {{ill|Submarine|en|Submarine|WD=Q2811|lt=Submarine|1=Submarine}} {{ship|Japanese submarine|Ro-101||2}} he was deployed on was fired on by the destroyer {{USS|Taylor|DD-468|6}} in {{ill|Indispensable Strait|en|Indispensable Strait|WD=Q2074010|lt=Indispensable Strait|1=Indispensable Strait}} near {{ill|Guadalcanal|en|Guadalcanal|WD=Q192767|lt=Guadalcanal|1=Guadalcanal}} in the {{ill|Solomon Islands|en|Solomon Islands|WD=Q685|lt=Solomon Islands|1=Solomon Islands}}. Shrapnel cut down Tokugawa and two enlisted lookouts, but the submarine was able to dive and escape. Tokugawa was posthumously promoted to the Rank of Lieutenant Commander.

